{"ts":"2026-10-23T01:55:52.13480603Z","session":"837b52b4-d41d-4919-9e09-c68083ddd2a3","parent_session":"837b52b4-d41d-4919-9e09-c68083ddd2a3","agent_id":"a3846b67ce53ea2ba","agent_type":"jms","delegation_id":"d-2026-10-22-185","contract_id":"m-2026-10-22-048","tool":"SubagentHandback","tool_input":{"message":"Committed as 289e971 on design/opencode-plugin-adapter. `make check` passed, including the fuzz type-check of docs/spec-opencode-lifecycle.tex. I did not push.\n\n**Results table**, each cell checked against its `.out` file in `.tmp/lc3/r6/`:\n- `MutA_claimed` is now a counterexample at 2818 states, depth 12 (trace length 12, ending LcCfReconcileClaimed). That matches the C4 trace in the .out and the prose.\n- `Reach_nosup` is now a counterexample at 218544 states, depth 17.\n- I changed the switches cell of `Reach_nosup` to \"all but Supersede and DurableName\". The .fuzz files show the only difference between `Reach_nosup` and `Reach_nosup_dur` is `fixDurableName` (zfalse against ztrue), so the old \"all but Supersede\" was wrong for `Reach_nosup`. This goes beyond the cells you listed.\n- New row `Reach_nosup_dur`: holds, all states visited, 257269 states, depth 24, switches \"all but Supersede\".\n\n**Limits section**, added to the paragraph \"What this model does not establish\":\n- N1, N2 and N3 cannot keep those numbers, because the document already uses N2, N3 and N4 to N15 in the consequences list and the limits paragraph. I numbered the three new items **N16, N17 and N18**, in the order you gave them. Say so if you want a different scheme.\n- N16 is your N1: release and close-time clearing run without a lock, and release is idempotent with no claim. The implementation must hold the child's dispatch-pending lock around the whole close, unname, clear sequence.\n- N17 is your N2: dispatch without a roster, the depth-gate close with verdict aborted, and a non-fatal binding-write failure.\n- N18 is your N3: \"release removes the record\" is hygiene, because `MyRelKeepRec` survives. The `pendDone` guard of `LcCfReconcileReuse` (`MutReuseDone`) is kept as already stated.\n- `MyRelKeepRec` appears nowhere else in the spec and has no .out file in `r6`, so I could not check it. N18 states it only as you described it.\n\n**Unrequested files in the commit:** it also contains two ethos runtime files, which the pre-commit audit-seal hook added to my commit:\n- `.punt-labs/ethos/missions/m-2026-10-22-048/log-837b52b4-...-1792719375495451327-1792719375495451327.jsonl`\n- `.punt-labs/ethos/sessions/2026-10-21-837b52b4-.../audit-1792719361705924724-1792720540177370273.jsonl`\n\nI did not stage or touch any other file."},"tool_input_hash":"8d8cbb95564bda82d70d8707a00a1258ba5adfb2418266844e0357371052c999","tool_input_preview":"{\"message\":\"Committed as 289e971 on design/opencode-plugin-adapter. `make check` passed, including the fuzz type-check of docs/spec-opencode-lifecycle.tex. I did not push.\\n\\n**Results table**, each c..."}
